      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "body": "I compared the notebook and script line-by-line against the template they were forked from. The notebook works correctly, but the script has three real bugs from an incomplete rename \u2014 it currently won't even run:\n\n**1. Broken `metrics` dict \u2014 `SyntaxError` (`3_finetune_template_1D.py:125-132`)**\n```python\nmetrics = {\n    train_loss_metrics = SolarEventMetrics(\"train_loss\")\n    ...\n}\n```\nThis mixes up the notebook's local-variable names (cell 26/38) with a dict literal \u2014 `=` instead of `:`, and no string keys. It won't parse. The notebook does this correctly in cell 38 (`'train_loss': train_loss_metrics, ...`). Should be:\n```python\nmetrics = {\n    \"train_loss\": SolarEventMetrics(\"train_loss\"),\n    \"val_loss\": SolarEventMetrics(\"val_loss\"),\n    \"train_metrics\": SolarEventMetrics(\"train_metrics\"),\n    \"val_metrics\": SolarEventMetrics(\"val_metrics\"),\n}\n```\n\n**2. `load_flare_config` never renamed \u2014 `NameError` (`3_finetune_template_1D.py:241`)**\n```python\ncfg = load_flare_config(args.config)\n```\nThe import at the top was correctly updated to `solar_event_config`, but this call site was missed \u2014 `load_flare_config` doesn't exist here anymore. The notebook (cell 5) correctly calls `solar_event_config(...)`. Fix: `cfg = solar_event_config(args.config)`.\n\n**3. `PATH_FIELDS` in `configs.py` still says the old field name**\n```python\nPATH_FIELDS: ClassVar[tuple[str, ...]] = DataConfig.PATH_FIELDS + (\"flare_index_path\",)\n```\nbut the actual field is `solar_event_path`. Since `flare_index_path` doesn't exist on `SolarDataConfig`, `_resolve_paths()` silently does nothing (`getattr(..., None)`), so `cfg.data.solar_event_path` is **never** resolved to an absolute path relative to the config file, per the CLAUDE.md contract that \"paths are relative to the config file.\" That's why both the notebook and script paper over it with `f\"data/{cfg.data.solar_event_path}\"` instead of just using `cfg.data.solar_event_path` directly (as the template does with `flare_index_path`).\n\nThis hack only happens to work in the notebook because its cwd is `downstream_apps/solar_event/`. Run the script the documented way (`python -m downstream_apps.solar_event.3_finetune_template_1D` from the repo root), and it resolves to `<repo_root>/data/solar_event_data2.csv` \u2014 which doesn't exist (the real file is at `downstream_apps/solar_event/data/solar_event_data2.csv`).\n\nProper fix: change `PATH_FIELDS` to `(\"solar_event_path\",)`, then simplify both call sites to `ds_flare_index_path=cfg.data.solar_event_path`.\n\nMinor (non-functional): the script's module docstring (lines 13-14) still says `downstream_apps.template.3_finetune_template_1D`.\n\nWant me to apply these fixes?",
